# Exp45 — Conditional Exit-Side Transport Confirmation — FROZEN

Frozen 2026-08-13 after Exp44 completion and before any Exp45 conditional-side score.

## Scientific question

Given that an eligible state has experienced its first corridor exit by a frozen horizon, does the exact already-frozen `POSITION_SURV` law improve prediction of WHICH SIDE (`ADVANCE` vs `RECAPTURE`) relative to `BASE_SURV` across all eight frozen direction×time environments, without any refit or new feature?

This isolates the side component suggested by Exp40-44. It is a predictive factorization test, not a causal claim and not a new predictor search.

## Frozen predictions

Use the exact original Exp41 TRAIN-fitted cumulative probabilities unchanged:

```text
BASE_SURV:     CIF_ADV_BASE(H), CIF_REC_BASE(H)
POSITION_SURV: CIF_ADV_POS(H),  CIF_REC_POS(H)
```

For an eligible state-horizon cell whose observed label is `ADVANCE` or `RECAPTURE`, define conditional side probability:

```text
q_ADV_BASE = CIF_ADV_BASE / (CIF_ADV_BASE + CIF_REC_BASE)
q_ADV_POS  = CIF_ADV_POS  / (CIF_ADV_POS  + CIF_REC_POS)
```

Observed binary target:

```text
y_side = 1 for ADVANCE
         0 for RECAPTURE
```

`NO_EXIT` cells are excluded by definition because Exp45 conditions on realized exit by that horizon. This exclusion is fixed before score and cannot be changed after result.

No new fit. No recalibration. No Dwell.

## Frozen environments and horizons

Reuse exactly Exp44 joint environments and frozen horizons `15/30/60/120m`.

Primary within each joint environment:

```text
SIDE_STATE_HORIZON_WEIGHTED pooled across all four horizons among observed exit cells
uncertainty = whole-BRT-day bootstrap preserving all exit cells for environment/day
```

A joint environment is formally scorable only if both ADVANCE and RECAPTURE are present and at least two BRT days contribute exit cells; otherwise status is `UNDERPOWERED_SIDE_ENVIRONMENT`, not PASS/FAIL.

## Frozen formal gate

Compare `q_ADV_POS` vs `q_ADV_BASE` with binary Brier and binary LogLoss.

Required in all 8 joint environments:

```text
gain = loss(BASE) - loss(POSITION)
CI95 lower bound > 0
```

Thus 16 mandatory proper-score cells.

```text
CONDITIONAL_SIDE_POSITION_TRANSPORT=PASS only if all 16 cells pass
ROBUST_WHICH_SIDE_LAW=PASS only if every environment is scorable and all 16 cells pass
```

## Diagnostics only

```text
exit-cell counts and ADV/REC rates
horizon-specific point gains
conditional SIDE AUC BASE->POSITION
conditional calibration by horizon/environment
descriptive UP-DOWN and EARLY-LATE gain differences
```

Diagnostics cannot rescue formal inference.

## Anti-rescue

```text
NO alternate conditioning event
NO NO_EXIT reweighting/rescue
NO alternate horizon subset
NO dropping joint environment
NO side-specific or era-specific fit
NO direction/time interaction
NO recalibration/intercept/threshold
NO alternate Position transform
NO Dwell rescue
NO Exp38/39 or D1/Clock/Z/Fib/weekday/Scale/Energy/HMM context
NO VAL/TEST refit
NO Exp27 scoring/modification
```

Exp45 failure cannot erase Exp44 `ROBUST_POSITION_CORE=PASS`. Historical OOS remains exploratory; runtime promotion NONE.
